.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
*.log
# generated by tools/selftest.py from the real index.html -- never edit or commit it, the whole
# point is that it cannot drift from the page it is testing
_selftest.html
.claude/
_lvaudit.html
_shots/
shots/
_shot.html
_measure.html
# generated by tools/audit.py around whichever _*audit.js it was asked for -- same rule as above
_audit_run.html

# tools/audit.py imports selftest.py for its Chrome discovery
tools/__pycache__/
# generated by tools/terrshot.py from the real index.html -- same rule as _selftest.html
_terrshot_run.html
_lab.html
_admincheck.html

# tools/mountinstall.py keeps the set it replaced here. Git already has the old pixels in history,
# so committing them again would just double the art in the repo -- but keep them ON DISK, because
# an art swap is the one change no selftest can judge and reverting has to be a copy, not a fetch.
assets/mounts/_old/

# The per-archetype "rider" layers, which were never riders -- each is the whole animal with a
# knight on it, and drawing one put a second smaller mount inside the real one. Out of the repo so
# nothing can read them again; kept on disk because they are still the only source a real rider
# layer could be extracted FROM. tools/mountart.py fails any that come back.
assets/riders/_composites/

# Rider layers extracted but not yet reviewed. The user asked for one mount at a time, so an
# archetype waits here until its own pass; moving it up one level is what makes it live.
assets/riders/_pending/

# Ridden sets that were generated and rejected. Kept on disk so a judgement can be revisited without
# spending generations again; out of the repo because they are not art the game should ever load.
assets/mounts/_old/

# generated by the stable shot rig, same rule as _shot.html and _audit_run.html
_stableshot.html

# _spritelab_index.json IS COMMITTED, deliberately, and this note is here so nobody re-adds it.
# It is generated (tools/spritelab.py rewrites it on every run), and the usual rule for generated
# files here is "never commit, it cannot then drift". This one is the exception because the Sprite
# Lab is served to a phone over the PUBLIC PAGES SITE, and a static host has no tool to run -- an
# ignored index means the hosted lab has no sources at all and comes up empty. Regenerated locally
# every time you open the lab, so the committed copy only lags for the hosted one; spritelab.py
# says so when it notices a difference.
_labparity.html
